From 1c7b2835570b33b3941995f0957e7185c2eaa480 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chang An <chang.an_1@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:14:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] bluetooth: classic: add OPP profile

Add the Object Push Profile (OPP) v1.1 with the Push Client and Push
Server roles, on GOEP v1.1 (OBEX over RFCOMM) and IrOBEX v1.2. Single
Response Mode, reliable sessions and OBEX over L2CAP are GOEP v2.0
features that the OPP ICS only allows from OPP v1.2 on, so they are not
supported.

The application builds the headers of each request and response. The
profile checks outgoing requests and responses, and the requests the
server receives, against OPP spec Table 5.2 and Table 5.3 and the IrOBEX
rules, and refuses those that break them. A push without an object
body, which IrOBEX treats as a delete request, is refused, as OPP has
no delete feature.

Tested on mimxrt1170_evk/mimxrt1176/cm7.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Chang An <chang.an_1@nxp.com>
